ly going to need  some more storage so the s21 ultra  basically means that if you buy the 128  gigabyte model  one hour of recording and that's it your  phone is full  you can basically dump that footage onto  a computer take it off  start again yes you can probably get rid  of a few apps and give  that a bit more storage but in actual  reality if you were to use your phone  unrestricted you'd probably only get  about an hour of recording now if you  put that  one terabyte sd card into the s20 ultra  which you can do on the s20 and you  can't do on the s21  you would get an additional 27.7  hours of 8k recording there's probably  no chance that you're going to go a  whole day  of recording without being close to a  laptop to dump that footage  if you need to so being able to have  almost  30 hours of recordable space on your  device  and still use your device to its full  capabilities is phenomenal  now if we backtrack and only look at the  4k video capabilities  at 30 frames a second 30 frames a second  4k  takes up 280 megabytes of storage  per one minute which equates to 16.8  gigabytes per hour  if again we use the same calculations 92  gigs of space  used through data downloads etc 128  gigabyte model  that gives you two hours of 4k video  recording  alternatively if you move up to the 256  gigabyte model  that gives you an extra 7.6 hours of  recording  whereas if you had the extra terabyte of  sd card storage you'd get  60 hours of 4k video recording so video  recording is very important to you  and storage is very important to you  you're either going to have to pay that  premium price tag for the 512 gigabyte  model  of the s21 ultra or stick with the s20  ultra for the simple fact that you have  that expandable storage  and for those fails with the s20 ultra  you can simply pop out that sd card put  a new sd card in  and keep recording you basically have no  limit  your only limit is the battery life  itself which brings us to another pretty  critical and important point  the s21 ultra might seem like the brand  new superior phone  but it has a few drawbacks so the s20  ultra in 30 minutes has the ability to  charge to 62  thanks to a 45 watt charging  capabilities whilst the s21 ultra is  limited to 25 watts of fast charging  and it can only fulfill 50 percent of  its battery life  within the first 30 minutes speaking of  charge times it's no good having a good  charger or a fast charging capability  if they don't actually include it in the  box so that price tag before  of 1849 i think it was  is actually a bit of a lie because you  need to go out and buy that additional  charger if you don't already have one  now as a youtuber you might also be  using a gimbal quite often  if you take the dji om4 for example  which is my gimbal of choice it has a  maximum payload of 230 grams  for the smartphone itself the s20 ultra  comes in at 220 grams whilst the s21  ultra comes in at 229 grams  so you're definitely putting the gimbal  at maximum payload capacity  but it is still able to be used on a  gimbal right now  there are some additional perks of the  s21 and it's the simple fact that the  screen resolution can now be used  at its best whereas the s20 is limited  and we still don't have that ability to  do so  the s21 has all the directors modes as  well as a vlogger mode where you can  record both  rear and front camera simultaneously it  also has  the s pen support which could or could  not be beneficial  to youtubers i think as a general rule  of thumb it's probably a nice little  feature to have but it's not necessary  and it is cheaper  there has been no price drop as of  recording this video  for the s20 ultra compared to the s21  ultra so if you would go out and store  and pick up either one of these two  devices the s20 would still be more  expensive so overall what's my opinion  well personally i believe if you already  have an s20 ultra  keep it for a couple more months till  some better deals come out on the s21  there is a number of deals that always  come out on samsung products especially  when the device has been out for a  little bit  and all those promotions go away for  pre-ordering if you're a youtuber  looking to do lots of studio setup  videos  and things where you have controlled  lighting and a controlled environment  i believe the s20 is phenomenal however  if you are a vlogger that's going to go  outside  constantly change camera angles  constantly be moving i think that laser  autofocus is almost a must  and it is definitely the platform and  the device of choice  anyway that's all for me today guys  thank you so much for watching i hope  you enjoyed the video if you did  make sure you smash that subscribe  button down below and as always i will  see you  next monday
 

